# ============================================================
# .gitattributes
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# The important line in this file is the one that is NOT there: PDFs are
# deliberately NOT tracked by Git LFS.
#
#   *.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text     ← do not add this
#
# The site is deployed from public/, which the builder fills by COPYING the
# PDFs in src/static/ (build.js step 4). Git LFS stores such a file as a
# 130-byte pointer in the working tree and keeps the bytes in a separate
# batch — and actions/checkout does NOT fetch LFS objects unless it is told
# to (lfs: true). So an LFS-tracked minutes file would be copied into the
# Pages artifact as a pointer, and visitors would download a text file where
# a PDF should be. check.sh now sniffs the %PDF- header and fails the build
# if that ever happens; this comment is why it exists.
#
# LFS would also add a quota to a site that has none: the free tier is about
# 1 GiB of storage AND 1 GiB of bandwidth per month, and every CI checkout
# that fetches LFS spends the bandwidth. Large documents that genuinely need
# it belong outside the site instead — docs/authoring.md §2d.
# ============================================================

# Text files are stored with LF in the repository (matches .editorconfig).
* text=auto

# Everything below is binary: never diff it, never merge it, never touch a
# byte of it. (The minutes PDFs in src/static/minutes/ are the reason this
# section exists; the images are already in src/assets/img/.)
*.pdf  -text
*.png  -text
*.jpg  -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif  -text
*.webp -text
*.ico  -text
*.woff -text
*.woff2 -text
*.zip  -text

# SVG is XML, i.e. text — say so explicitly, because the rule above could
# otherwise be extended to "everything in assets/img" by mistake.
*.svg  text
